{'symbol': 'COF', 'date': '2021-04-27 16:05:00', 'title': 'CAPITAL ONE REPORTS FIRST QUARTER 2021 NET INCOME OF $3.3 BILLION, OR $7.03 PER SHARE', 'text': 'MCLEAN, VA., APRIL 27, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION (NYSE: COF) TODAY ANNOUNCED NET INCOME FOR THE FIRST QUARTER OF 2021 OF $3.3 BILLION, OR $7.03 PER DILUTED COMMON SHARE, COMPARED WITH NET INCOME OF $2.6 BILLION, OR $5.35 PER DILUTED COMMON SHARE IN THE FOURTH QUARTER OF 2020, AND WITH A NET LOSS OF $1.3 BILLION, OR $3.10 PER DILUTED COMMON SHARE IN THE FIRST QUARTER OF 2020.'}